# SQL's uppercase `WHERE`: DS0105, with a fix to `where`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | WHERE amount > 10
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..38
  PIPELINE@0..37
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..37
      IDENT@20..25 "WHERE"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..37
        NAME_REF@26..32
          IDENT@26..32 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
        GT@33..34 ">"
        WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
        LITERAL@35..37
          LONG@35..37 "10"
  WHITESPACE@37..38 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `WHERE` is not an operator
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | WHERE amount > 10
  |                     ^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: operator names are lowercase: write `where`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where amount > 10
which parses without errors
